extraction_notes: |
  - Underseas, printed 55-56. The mystic of the three Pneuma-Biforms, with
    the strongest magic of any Whale Singer or any creation of the Lord of
    the Deep, and the only one of the three that is a MASTER psionic with a
    real grant rather than a percentile roll.
  - ITS M.D.C. AND SIZE VARY BY WHALE SPECIES AND ONLY ONE FIGURE IS STORED.
    Printed 55 gives three M.D.C. formulas - blue, sperm/large, beaked/medium
    - and the sperm/large one is stored as the middle case. All three are in
    the restrictions. This is NOT modelled as `variants`, because the three
    differ only in two numbers and a variant replaces a whole block; a note
    a player can act on is the smaller and more honest shape.
  - THE LEVEL-ONE OCEAN GRANT IS A CHOICE THE APP CANNOT OFFER. Printed 55
    gives any three ocean spells OR dolphin magic instead. Three ocean spells
    is stored and the alternative is in the starting group''s note, because a
    starting group picks from one list and cannot branch.
  - IT GETS NO FREE HAND TO HAND. Printed 56 makes every combat skill cost
    related-skill selections, on a sliding scale. There is no key for a skill
    that costs more than one pick, so the rule is a restriction line.
  - THE SING BONUS IS SPECIES-DEPENDENT: +10% generally and +20% for a
    humpback. The general figure is stored.
  - ATTACKS ARE TWO IN EITHER FORM, which is the same figure both ways - the
    only one of the three biforms where human and cetacean forms agree.
