# Pneuma-Biform Whale

## Lore

The mystics of the cetacean order are the pneuma-biform whales, who have the strongest magic powers of any Whale Singer and of any creation of the Lord of the Deep. They are the leaders and guides of the other biforms, and the deepest thinkers among them.

The dolphins and orcas sometimes criticise them for being too thoughtful, and too slow to act until the right answer has been found. To which the PB-whales reply that the Lord of the Deep was here before they were born and will likely be here after they are gone - unless somebody thinks things through.

A PB-whale may be any species of whale, and the difference is not cosmetic: a blue whale biform is a hundred feet long and carries several times the mega-damage of a beaked one.

## GM Notes

Besides the Whale Singers, PB-whales often team up with other biforms, sea druids, ocean mages and normal dolphins and whales. They tend to avoid regular contact with surface dwellers and aquatic humanoids, but will work with or befriend humans, sea titans, amphibs, sea inquisitors and anyone of good alignment or good intentions.

They rely on their natural powers in both forms. A few own magical or rune weapons and items. Body armour is usually none except in human disguise, occasionally magically woven kelp armour of 90 M.D.C. from the Song of Weaving.

Most keep a small cache for walking among men - a weapon or four, some simple clothing and assorted odds and ends.
